      "text": "infinite",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Now we know that maximum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi></math>&nbsp;function is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>M</mi></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now equating both to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now solving&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now solving&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;we get&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Now from equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we can see common solution is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Hence, possible solution is only one.</p></blockquote>"
  }
